  <h2>The \"Unlimited\" Reality: Dynamic Rate Limits</h2>
  <p>OpenAI's documentation states ChatGPT Pro has \"no hard caps\" but enforces <strong>dynamic rate limits</strong> to prevent abuse. Community telemetry (Reddit, Discord, developer forums) suggests:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>o1 / o1-pro:</strong> ~200–500 messages/day before throttle (rolling 3-hour window)</li>
    <li><strong>GPT-4o:</strong> ~1,000+ messages/day (rarely hit)</li>
    <li><strong>Codex in ChatGPT:</strong> Counts toward o1/GPT-4o limits depending on model selected</li>
    <li><strong>Reset cadence:</strong> Rolling 3-hour window (not daily midnight reset)</li>
  </ul>
  <p><strong>Critical:</strong> These are community estimates. OpenAI publishes no SLA, no fixed quotas, and no per-seat guarantees. Limits adjust based on system load.</p>

  <h2>Codex: What's Included vs What's Not</h2>
  <h3>Included in ChatGPT Pro ($200)</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Codex agent in ChatGPT web UI (uses o1/GPT-4o from Pro pool)</li>
    <li>Codex in ChatGPT mobile/desktop apps</li>
    <li>File upload, code execution, web search within Codex sessions</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>NOT Included — Billed at API Rates</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Codex CLI</strong> (terminal agent) — every call bills at o1/GPT-4o API rates</li>
    <li><strong>Codex API</strong> (programmatic access) — standard API pricing</li>
    <li><strong>Batch API, Assistants API, Realtime API</strong> — all separate billing</li>
  </ul>
  <p style="background:#101726;padding:12px;border-radius:6px;border-left:4px solid #FF6B6B;color:#E6EAF2;">
    <strong>Common misconception:</strong> \"ChatGPT Pro includes Codex CLI.\" It does not. Codex CLI is an API product. Engineers using Codex CLI daily will incur significant API charges on top of the $200 Pro subscription.
  </p>

  <h2>API-Equivalent Valuation</h2>
  <p>At o1 pricing ($15/M input, $60/M output), the $200 Pro subscription breaks even at:</p>
  <p style="background:#101726;padding:12px;border-radius:6px;font-family:monospace;color:#7AAFFF;text-align:center;">
    Break-even ≈ 1.33M input tokens + 200k output tokens / month (o1)
  </p>
  <p>Typical o1 coding session: ~8k input + 2k output tokens (including reasoning).</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>50 o1 sessions/day × 20 days = 1,000 sessions/mo</strong> → ~8M in + 2M out tokens → ~$240 API cost → <strong>Pro saves ~$40/mo</strong></li>
    <li><strong>100 o1 sessions/day × 20 days = 2,000 sessions/mo</strong> → ~16M in + 4M out → ~$480 API cost → <strong>Pro saves ~$280/mo</strong></li>
    <li><strong>10 o1 sessions/day</strong> → ~$48 API cost → <strong>API direct is cheaper</strong></li>
  </ul>

