  <h3>Team of 5: Cost Scenarios</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>All API direct:</strong> Variable. Estimate $150–400/mo per heavy engineer.</li>
    <li><strong>3× Pro + 2× API:</strong> $600 + $300–800 = $900–1,400/mo — mixed team.</li>
    <li><strong>5× Pro:</strong> $1,000/mo — only justified if all 5 are heavy o1/Codex UI users.</li>
    <li><strong>Hybrid:</strong> Pro for ChatGPT/Codex UI users; API budget for CLI/automation.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Hidden Costs & Gotchas</h2>
  <h3>1. Codex CLI ≠ Pro Subscription</h3>
  <p>This is the #1 billing surprise. Engineers assume Pro covers everything \"Codex.\" It doesn't. Codex CLI usage at 50 sessions/day ≈ $150–300/mo in API charges <em>on top of</em> the $200 Pro fee.</p>

  <h3>2. Reasoning Tokens Count at Output Rates</h3>
  <p>o1's internal reasoning tokens are billed at <strong>output token rates ($60/M)</strong>. A single complex o1 task can generate 10k–50k reasoning tokens. At 50 tasks/day, that's 500k–2.5M reasoning tokens/day → $30–150/day in reasoning alone.</p>

  <h3>3. No Prompt Caching Discount in Pro</h3>
  <p>API users get 50% cache-read discount on o1 ($7.50/M vs $15/M). Pro users cannot control or measure cache hits — the dynamic pool manages it opaquely.</p>

  <h3>4. No Off-Peak or Volume Discounts</h3>
  <p>Unlike Alibaba Token Pro (0.2× off-peak) or Anthropic API (batch 50% discount), OpenAI offers no time-of-day or volume discounts on Pro or API.</p>

  <h3>5. Shared Account Pool Risk</h3>
  <p>Pro limits are per-account, not per-seat in a team workspace. One engineer's heavy o1-pro usage can throttle teammates on the same Pro account.</p>

