  <h2>FinOps Recommendation</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Audit actual usage first.</strong> Pull 30-day Codex CLI + ChatGPT API logs per engineer before buying Pro.</li>
    <li><strong>Buy Pro only for heavy ChatGPT/Codex UI users</strong> (≥30 o1 sessions/day). Light users: API direct.</li>
    <li><strong>Budget Codex CLI separately.</strong> It is not covered by Pro. Allocate API budget for CLI/automation.</li>
    <li><strong>Track reasoning token spend.</strong> o1 reasoning at $60/M output is the hidden cost driver. Monitor per-engineer.</li>
    <li><strong>No team pooling.</strong> Pro is per-account. Don't share one Pro seat across multiple engineers.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Bottom Line for CFOs</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>ChatGPT Pro ($200) = o1/Codex UI subscription.</strong> Codex CLI, API, automation = separate API budget.</li>
    <li><strong>Break-even: ~50 o1 sessions/day.</strong> Below that, API direct is cheaper. Above that, Pro saves 60%+.</li>
    <li><strong>Reasoning tokens are expensive.</strong> o1 reasoning at $60/M output can dominate spend. Monitor it.</li>
    <li><strong>No volume/off-peak discounts.</strong> $200/mo flat regardless of usage pattern.</li>
    <li><strong>Seat = account.</strong> One Pro per engineer. No sharing, no pooling.</li>
  </ul>